Hands-On Challenge 1: Custom Field Creation
Theory

In Salesforce, custom fields are used to store additional business-specific information that is not available in standard fields. Creating custom fields helps organizations customize objects according to their requirements without writing code.

In this challenge, a Currency field named Loan Amount was created in the Contact object to store customer loan eligibility amounts. This improves customer data management and helps brokers easily identify the customer’s budget range.

Objective

Create a custom field in the Contact object.

Steps Performed
Opened Setup
Navigated to Object Manager → Contact
Opened Fields & Relationships
Created a new Currency field
Field Details
Field Label: Loan Amount
Field Name: Loan_Amount
Field Type: Currency
Result

Successfully created a custom field to store customer loan amounts.


